{"abstract":[{"text":"A Google Drive cloud backend for Ensembles.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"EnsemblesGoogleDrive"}],"role":"collection","title":"EnsemblesGoogleDrive","roleHeading":"Framework","externalID":"EnsemblesGoogleDrive","symbolKind":"module"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/EnsemblesGoogleDrive\/documentation\/EnsemblesGoogleDrive\/GoogleDriveCloudFileSystem","doc:\/\/EnsemblesGoogleDrive\/documentation\/EnsemblesGoogleDrive\/GoogleDriveAuthenticator"],"title":"Cloud File System","anchor":"Cloud-File-System"}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"EnsemblesGoogleDrive provides ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/EnsemblesGoogleDrive\/documentation\/EnsemblesGoogleDrive\/GoogleDriveCloudFileSystem","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", an implementation of the Ensembles "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CloudFileSystem"},{"text":" protocol that stores sync data on Google Drive. It communicates directly with the Google Drive REST API v3 using ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession"},{"type":"text","text":" — no third-party SDK required."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Google Drive uses file IDs rather than paths internally. The backend transparently bridges between Ensembles’ path-based "},{"code":"CloudFileSystem","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" protocol and Google Drive’s ID-based system, caching folder and file IDs to minimize API calls.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Authentication","anchor":"Authentication","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The included ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/EnsemblesGoogleDrive\/documentation\/EnsemblesGoogleDrive\/GoogleDriveAuthenticator"},{"text":" handles the full OAuth 2.0 authorization code flow, stores tokens in the